source: tests/ui/lint/mod.rs
---
  ▲ Zero replacement count
   ╭─[test.lis:6:11]
 5 │   let s = "banana"
 6 │   let _ = strings.Replace(s, "a", "b", (0))
   ·           ────────────────┬────────────────
   ·                           ╰── replaces nothing
 7 │ }
   ╰────
  help: `strings.Replace` with a count of `0` replaces nothing and returns `s` unchanged. Use `strings.ReplaceAll(s, "a", "b")` to replace every occurrence, or a positive count to replace that many · code: [lint.replace_count_zero]
